Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||11-16-2000||01:15 PM||||I've owned my domain (www.starhero.com) for a few months now. It is primarily for promotion of the book I am writing. However, I know that many people like to follow the progress of other members' cars as they are rebuilt, and I would like to post those updates to my site as they come.<P>The sticking point in the middle of all of this is, where to get a reasonably priced host with enough features and bandwidth? I definitely don't want a freebie site, as they have those (incredibly) annoying popup windows. And it has to be my domain, as when I finally get this book done, starhero.com will be easy enough to remember.<P>So, for those who have their own domain names, where do you host, and how much is it?<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||LarryB||11-16-2000||05:40 PM||||<BR>Since you're in the metro Boston area I'll point you to <A HREF="http://www.shore.net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.shore.net</A>  as a good starting point.  They can set you up with space on a shared server, host your domain for you, and give you bandwidth allocation for a pretty low rate.<P>[I have no affiliation with them, they would in fact be viewed as a potential bandwidth customer by my employer.]<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Patrick's Dad:<BR><B>I've owned my domain (www.starhero.com) for a few months now. It is primarily for promotion of the book I am writing. However, I know that many people like to follow the progress of other members' cars as they are rebuilt, and I would like to post those updates to my site as they come.<P>The sticking point in the middle of all of this is, where to get a reasonably priced host with enough features and bandwidth? I definitely don't want a freebie site, as they have those (incredibly) annoying popup windows. And it has to be my domain, as when I finally get this book done, starhero.com will be easy enough to remember.<P>So, for those who have their own domain names, where do you host, and how much is it?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
